# Truncates the container logs once per session, before any container starts.
# Growth is otherwise unbounded (~160 KB/day for navidrome alone) because
# dinit does not rotate a logfile and Chimera ships no logrotate.
#
# Deliberately a dependency rather than a `: > log` prefixed to each
# container's own command: `restart = yes` would re-run that on every restart
# and erase the crash output of a looping container. A dependency starts once
# and is not re-run when the dependent process restarts.
type = scripted
command = /home/evan/.config/scripts/truncate-container-logs
